body:
Yes but it adds not needed extra logic.

Some suggestions:

``` php
$field = $builder->create('individualQuestionOptions', 'choice', array(
    // 'data_class' => IndividualQuestionOption::class, guessed
    // 'multiple' => false, default
    'expanded' => true,
    // 'auto_initialize' => false, internal only true for root form
    'choices' => $question->getIndividualQuestionOptions(),
    // 'translation_domain' => 'validators', default for error messages
    // 'empty_value' => false, default since required is true by default and you use radio inputs
    'choices_as_values' => true,
));

// Lazy way :)
$field->addModelTransformer(new \Symfony\Bridge\Doctrine\Form\DataTransformer\CollectionToArrayTransformer());
```

The `CollectionToArrayTransformer` is a bit different from my `ChoiceToQuestionOptionTransformer` ;) Does not really work.

With this addition it now works again for me:

``` php
'choice_label' => function(IndividualQuestionOption $option) {
    return (string) $option;
}
```
